      "name": "d5-article-review",
      "version": "1.1.0",
      "description": "Three-gate sign-off judge for D5 articles: the reviewer who decides publish-or-hold, not a second QA pass. One read, three parallel gates, any gate failing = HOLD, no cross-compensation: 1) Content value — what does the reader take away, or is it just another ad? (time-worth test: save / share / act); 2) Brand fidelity — could any render vendor have written this, or does it carry D5's fingerprints (Protecting the Flow, no marketing tone, no AI flavor); 3) SEO — searchable, clickable, retainable (intent match + facade + content depth). Output is deliberately minimal: three one-line verdicts + one decision (READY / HOLD). Bundle includes intake template, review prompt, and output template — adapt the gates to your own product's brand ammo and banned-phrase list.",
